{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790961222,"nonce":"6BoneXP3yZERYD0bqT45T/NAs1A=","title":"Orphaned exports: --adopt DURATION and consolidation by first sync","message":"A Jira issue created by an export names its local entity in a property. A clone meeting it without that entity skipped it (pull first), which is right while the entity is on its way and wrong for good when the exporting store is gone: the skip was reported once, every child waiting on it was re-read each run and reported without the cause, and nothing adopted it. Seen: 47 orphans blocking 66 children.\n\nDecided (doc/design/jira-sync.md, JS27): no observable separates in flight from lost, so the bound is the person's, `--adopt DURATION`, on Jira's clock against the issue's created. Skipped orphans are remembered in the state file and named as the cause on each waiting child. Two local copies of one Jira issue are consolidated into the one that reached Jira first (earliest jira-create attempt or marker Updated, an export before an import at one second, then the lower id), ignoring the archived flag so every clone agrees: the loser is synced once more, archived, its local-only values carried over, and every relation naming it re-pointed.\n\nTests: jira/orphan_test.go E26-E28.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["bridge"],"parent":"8ade81134de7c2f5d1a16c3a48efc761b35bbf4cc2a58eaf8189fa5c15621e01","priority":"high","status":"to-do","type":"task"}}]}